# Copy to .env for local development. The portal reads the bot's database —
# point this at the same MySQL/MariaDB instance discord-bot uses (or, for a
# quick local loop, the throwaway container from discord-bot's README).
DATABASE_URL=mysql://root:rootpassword@127.0.0.1:3399/discord_bot_test_d
PORT=3001

# >>>> ADMIN OAUTH (M8.10, optional) >>>>
# Leave every one of these unset for local dev with no admin surface — every
# public page/route works with nothing set here (src/lib/discordAuth.ts's
# loadOAuthConfig() returns null and /api/auth/*, /api/admin/* answer 503),
# the same "degrades safely" contract discord-bot's own DISCORD_TOKEN has
# (see AGENT.md "Traps"). To exercise the admin login locally:
#
#  1. Discord Developer Portal (https://discord.com/developers/applications) ->
#     the Game On Portugal application (same app as DISCORD_CLIENT_ID in
#     discord-bot/.env.example) -> OAuth2 -> add a redirect:
#       http://localhost:3001/api/auth/callback         (local dev)
#       https://game-on-portugal.pt/api/auth/callback   (production — see
#         infrastructure/game-on-portugal.yaml's portal-api service)
#  2. OAuth2 -> "Client Secret" -> Reset Secret -> copy it into
#     DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET below (or the Portainer stack env in prod). This
#     is the one genuinely new secret M8.10 needs; DISCORD_CLIENT_ID is
#     already public (it's in every OAuth authorize URL) and already set for
#     the bot.
#
# DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id           # same value as discord-bot's DISCORD_CLIENT_ID
# DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret   # NEW secret — Discord Developer Portal, OAuth2 tab
# DISCORD_GUILD_ID=818108848492773377        # defaults to this if unset — the verified production guild
#
# Signs/verifies the admin session cookie (see src/lib/session.ts) — there is
# no session table, so this secret alone is what makes a session
# unforgeable. Generate with `openssl rand -hex 32`. Rotating it instantly
# logs out every admin (all existing cookies stop verifying) — that is a
# feature, not a bug, if a secret ever leaks.
# SESSION_SECRET=
# SESSION_TTL_HOURS=12
# <<<< ADMIN OAUTH <<<<

# >>>> AUDIT LOG (M8.11, optional) >>>>
# Every admin write (ad edit/expire/delete, screenshot delete, trophy-profile
# ban/exclude) is recorded here — a private SQLite file this service owns
# outright (src/audit/db.ts explains why not a MySQL table). Defaults to
# ./data/audit.db; the Portainer stack mounts a volume at that path (see
# infrastructure/game-on-portugal.yaml's portal-api service) so it survives
# redeploys. Not a secret — no need to set this locally.
# AUDIT_DB_PATH=./data/audit.db
# <<<< AUDIT LOG <<<<

# >>>> THUMBNAILS (M8.8, optional) >>>>
# GET /api/media/thumbnail?src=<origin url>&w=<160|320|480> — resizes an
# origin screenshot/ad photo to a small fixed set of widths, re-encodes to
# WebP, and caches the result on disk (src/lib/thumbnails.ts). Not a secret;
# defaults to ./data/thumbnails, no need to set this locally. In production
# this shares the same portal_audit_data volume the audit log uses (see
# infrastructure/game-on-portugal.yaml) so the cache survives redeploys —
# losing it is harmless either way, it just costs one re-fetch+resize per
# entry the next time each thumbnail is requested.
# THUMBNAIL_CACHE_DIR=./data/thumbnails
#
# MEDIA_HOSTS / MEDIA_PATH_PREFIXES (src/lib/mediaAllowlist.ts): which origin
# URLs the thumbnail endpoint is willing to fetch at all — refusing anything
# else is what keeps this from being an open image proxy / SSRF hole.
# Default is exactly the production MinIO bucket; only change this for local
# dev against a differently-hosted MinIO.
# MEDIA_HOSTS=media.game-on-portugal.pt
# MEDIA_PATH_PREFIXES=/gop-media/
# <<<< THUMBNAILS <<<<

# >>>> CORS (optional) >>>>
# Only matters when portal-web and portal-api run as two separate processes/
# ports (local dev) — production is single-origin via nginx, see app.ts's
# header comment. Comma-separated allow-list; must include credentials for
# the admin session cookie to survive the cross-port fetch.
# CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173
# <<<< CORS <<<<

# >>>> WEB ORIGIN (optional) >>>>
# Where /api/auth/* should redirect back to after login/logout, and the base
# sitemap.xml URLs use. Defaults to this API's own origin, which is correct
# in production (single-origin) but wrong for local dev, where the web app is
# on a different port.
# WEB_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173
# <<<< WEB ORIGIN <<<<
